  "stages": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "title": "Locate the head",
      "text": "Locate the femoral head on this textbook illustration. Chapter forty-five identifies interruption of its blood supply as the initiating problem in Legg Calv\u00e9 Perthes disease."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.76,
      "title": "Necrosis and collapse",
      "text": "The supplied sequence is necrosis of the ossification center, collapse, and gradual remodeling by living bone. Watch the highlighted head lose its rounded contour. This deformation illustrates the described collapse; it does not reproduce a patient radiograph or predict the final shape."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.3,
      "title": "Remodeling and containment",
      "text": "The final stage illustrates remodeling without promising a complete return to the original contour. The packet\u2019s containment goal is to keep the ball completely within the socket, while maintaining motion. Knee pain can be part of this hip disorder. The source does not supply a precise recovery timeline for this animation."
    }
  ],
